.TH QCC 1 "2026 May 14" "Qore 3.0" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
qcc \- Qore ahead-of-time compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qcc
[\fIoptions\fP]
\fIsource-file\fP|\fIobject\fP...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBqcc\fR compiles Qore scripts, user modules, relocatable Qore objects, and
archives using Qore's IR and LLVM AOT backend.
It can produce standalone native executables, native \fB.qmod\fP user modules,
per-file \fB.qo\fP relocatable objects, and \fB.qoa\fP static archives.
.PP
AOT compilation requires \fB%modern\fP source semantics.
Modern script and application sources should use the \fB.qr\fP extension,
which enables \fB%modern\fP by default.
The \fB.q\fP extension keeps legacy defaults unless the source contains an
explicit \fB%modern\fP directive.
Other non-\fB.q\fP source extensions, such as \fB.qc\fP and \fB.qm\fP, also
enable \fB%modern\fP by default.
Cross-compilation requires LLVM support for the selected target.
Static linking requires a Qore build configured with
\fBBUILD_STATIC_LIBQORE=ON\fP.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Output Mode"
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIfile\fP
Set the output path.
If omitted, the input file name without its extension is used.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-opt\-level =\fIN\fP
Set LLVM optimization level 0 through 3.
The default is 3.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-module
Compile the input as a user module.
A single \fB.qm\fP file or a split module directory can be compiled to
\fB.qmod\fP.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compile\-only
Compile to a \fB.qo\fP relocatable object.
.TP
.B \-\-context =\fIdir\fP
Set the directory context for per-file \fB.qo\fP compilation.
This parses the whole split-module directory but emits only the selected
input file's contributions.
Required for some \fB\-c\fP workflows.
.TP
.BI \-L " dir"
Add a script-mode sibling \fB.qo\fP search path.
May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-dir =\fIdir\fP
Write compile-only output to \fIdir\fP.
Required for batch mode with multiple sources and mutually exclusive with
\fB\-o\fP.
Each \fB.qo\fP object is written atomically by compiling to a temporary file
and renaming it into place, so independent per-file \fB\-c\fP jobs writing into
the same directory may run in parallel (for example under \fBmake \-j\fP) and a
concurrent \fB\-L\fP sibling scan never observes a half-written object.
.TP
.B \-\-from\-objects
Aggregate mode.
Positional arguments are \fB.qo\fP inputs; requires \fB\-m\fP and
\fB\-\-context\fP and emits a standard \fB.qmod\fP.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-archive
Archive mode.
Positional arguments are \fB.qo\fP inputs; requires \fB\-\-context\fP and emits
a \fB.qoa\fP static archive exposing \fBqore_qoa_register_all()\fP for a C++
host.
.SS "Compile Context"
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-load =\fImodule\fP
Load a Qore module before parsing sources.
May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-stub =\fIfile\fP
Preload a declarative Qore source file before target sources.
The stub contributes declarations to parsing but does not emit a \fB.qo\fP.
May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-parse\-option =\fIname\fP
Add a parse option or \fBPO_*\fP flag to the compile program.
May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-define =\fIname\fP[=\fIvalue\fP]
Set a parser define before source parsing.
May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-depfile =\fIfile\fP
Emit a Make-format dependency file after a successful compile.
.TP
.B \-\-save\-temps
Keep temporary \fB.qo\fP objects and generated C++ glue from one-shot
multi-source executable mode.
.SS "Target and Link Options"
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-static
Link a single-source executable statically against libqore.
Generated-host modes, including one-shot multi-source executables and
\fB.qo\fP link mode, do not support \fB\-\-static\fP directly.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target =\fItriple\fP
Compile for an LLVM target triple instead of the native host target.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-targets
Show supported target architectures and exit.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-entry =\fIfunction\fP
Set the Qore function called by the generated C++ \fBmain()\fP in one-shot
multi-source executable mode or \fB.qo\fP link mode.
The default is \fBmain\fP.
.SS "Metadata and Debug Information"
.TP
.B \-\-include\-source
Embed source text in AOT metadata.
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-source
Strip source text from AOT metadata.
This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-debug\-info
Do not emit DWARF debug information.
This reduces compile time and output size but disables debugger source/line
support.
.TP
.B \-g
Emit DWARF debug information.
This is the default and overrides \fB\-\-strip\-debug\-info\fP when both are
specified.
.TP
.B \-\-time\-trace[=\fIpath\fP]
Emit a Chrome trace JSON file for optimization and code-generation passes.
The default path is \fBqcc.trace.json\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-big\-fn\-threshold =\fIN\fP
Mark functions with at least \fIN\fP IR blocks as \fBOptimizeNone\fP and
\fBNoInline\fP.
This trades some runtime speed for substantially faster compilation of very
large functions.
The default is 200; use 0 to disable.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-warnings\-are\-errors
Treat Qore parser warnings as fatal compile errors.
.SS "Inspection"
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-info
Inspect embedded Qore AOT metadata in object files, \fB.qmod\fP modules,
\fB.qo\fP fragments, \fB.qoa\fP archives, or linked AOT executables without
executing them.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-symbols
With \fB\-\-dump\-info\fP, include an nm-like symbol table view.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-sections
With \fB\-\-dump\-info\fP, include object and AOT section tables.
.SS "General"
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print verbose compiler progress.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QORE_LIBDIR
Directory containing libqore.
\fBqcc\fP uses this when locating the runtime library for generated code.
.TP
.B QORE_INCLUDE_DIR
Colon-separated list of include directories.
.TP
.B QORE_INCLUDE_DIRS
Additional colon-separated include directories.
.TP
.B QORE_AOT_BIG_FN_THRESHOLD
Default threshold used by \fB\-\-big\-fn\-threshold\fP when the option is not
specified.
.TP
.B QORE_AOT_NO_DEBUG_INFO
If set to 1, disables AOT debug information unless overridden by command-line
options.
.TP
.B QORE_AOT_BATCH_JOBS
Number of worker threads used to emit \fB.qo\fP objects in batch
(\fB\-\-output\-dir\fP) mode.
The sources are parsed once on a single thread, then each object's code
generation runs on the pool, parallelizing the dominant \fB\-O3\fP backend.
Defaults to the number of hardware threads; set to 1 to emit serially.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compile a script to a native executable:
.RS
.B qcc script.qr
.RE
.PP
Compile a script with an explicit output path:
.RS
.B qcc -o myapp script.qr
.RE
.PP
Compile a multi-file application directly to an executable:
.RS
.B qcc -o myapp src/lib.qr src/main.qr
.RE
.PP
Batch-compile a multi-file application and link it:
.RS
.B qcc -c --output-dir=build/aot src/lib.qr src/main.qr
.br
.B qcc -o myapp build/aot/*.qo
.RE
.PP
Compile a split user module:
.RS
.B qcc -m qlib/DataProvider
.RE
.PP
Compile a source file to a relocatable Qore object:
.RS
.B qcc -c --context=qlib/MyModule qlib/MyModule/Part.qc
.RE
.PP
Inspect metadata in a compiled module:
.RS
.B qcc --dump-info MyModule.qmod
.RE
